  "details": "making forests look real is a real pain to make, since it always looks so artificial. \"generating\" these forests would make this artificial factor go away. So vegetation studio would make this artificial factor go away.\nVegetation studio is rule based vegetation system, where you can make a set of rules how the vegetation \"grows\". e.g. you can set that the trees and grass dont grow on rocks, you can make vegetation masks manually where you dont want vegetation to go. you can also make a masks on items (e.g. houses) so the vegetation always disappears around the house. it would make the world creation (especially nature maps) look better and also making it slightly easier. Vegetationstudio also has in-build culling system, that keeps the performance high in vegetation maps. (culling = disables the object rendering when they are not in field of view)",
